  "description": "T1  Purple Plum tree:  Reduce the crown by approximately 2-2.5 meters and remove dead or diseased wood. (Phellinus fungus throughout the crown). T2  Cotoneaster tree: Remove dead and dying sections only, no reduction recommended. T3  Catalpa tree : Reduce by approximately 1-1.5 metres, back to previous reduction points and to provide clearance from the buildings. Lift the canopy above the footpath up to approximately 3 meters above ground level and removed all dead or diseased wood. T4  North American Bud tree: Reduce by approximately 2-2.5 meters, back to previous reduction points and to clear the building. T5 Malus tree:  Reduce by approximately 1-1.5 meters, back to previous reduction points and remove any large dead or diseased wood. T6  Olive tree:  Reduce by approximately 50% / 2 meters. Remove the large top stems back down to the lower canopy and nip in the side growth to create as neat a dome shape as possible.",
